-- INTEGRATED PERSONALITY DEVELOPMENT COURSE-I | Mid 1 | easy | 460091640101011 | theory
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (460091640101011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Students learn how self-improvement enables them to secure a bright future for thems in the context of Remaking Yourself Restructuring Yourself. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Students will undergo a study of how habits work in the context of Remaking Yourself Power of Habit. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Students will learn from the inspirational lives of India''s two legends in the context of Learning from Legends- Tendulkar & Tata. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Active listening is an essential part of academic progress and communications. Stude in the context of From House to Home Listening & Understanding. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Students learn how self-improvement enables them to secure a bright future for thems is covered in “Remaking Yourself Restructuring Yourself”. A good answer should define its purpose, explain its main components or steps, connect it to Students learn how self-improvement enables them to secure a bright future for themselves. They will learn 6 powerful thought- processes that can develop their intellectual, physical, emotional, and spiritual quotients., provide a practical example and state how the result can be checked.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Students learn how self-improvement enables them to secure a bright future for themselves. They will learn 6 powerful thought- processes that can develop their intellectual; physical; emotional; and spiritual quotients.. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Integrated Personality Development Course-I problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Habits develop through repetition in a context. Effective habit-building uses clear cues, achievable actions and consistent feedback.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as the habits of successful professionals; and the practical techniques that can be used to develop good habits in their life.; Remaking Yourself Power of Habit. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Integrated Personality Development Course-I problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Students will learn from the inspirational lives of India''s two legends is covered in “Learning from Legends- Tendulkar & Tata”. A good answer should define its purpose, explain its main components or steps, connect it to Sachin Tendulkar and Ratan Tata. They will implement these lessons through relatable case studies., Learning from Legends- Tendulkar & Tata, provide a practical example and state how the result can be checked.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Sachin Tendulkar and Ratan Tata. They will implement these lessons through relatable case studies.; Learning from Legends- Tendulkar & Tata. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Integrated Personality Development Course-I problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Active listening requires focused attention, interpretation, clarification and feedback. It supports understanding by checking meaning instead of assuming.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Active listening is an essential part of academic progress and communications. Students will learn to listen with their eyes; ears; mind; and heart.. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Integrated Personality Development Course-I problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

