VALUES (460091312102011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Algebra of Matrices in the context of Determinants and Matrices. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain System of Linear Equation in the context of Equations. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Determinant of Matrix in the context of Determinants and Matrices. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Inverse of Matrix up to 3×3 matrix in the context of Determinants and Matrices. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** A determinant is a scalar associated with a square matrix; a non-zero determinant indicates invertibility.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Determinant of Matrix; Inverse of Matrix up to 3×3 matrix; Solution of Simultaneous Equation (up to 3 variable); Determinants and Matrices. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-II problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** System of Linear Equation is covered in “Equations”. A good answer should define its purpose, explain its main components or steps, connect it to Solution of Quadratic Equation, Solution of Cubic Equation, Equations, provide a practical example and state how the result can be checked.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Solution of Quadratic Equation; Solution of Cubic Equation; Equations. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-II problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** A matrix is a rectangular array. Matrix operations require compatible dimensions; square matrices may have determinants and inverses.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Algebra of Matrices; Inverse of Matrix up to 3×3 matrix; Solution of Simultaneous Equation (up to 3 variable); Determinants and Matrices. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-II problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** A matrix is a rectangular array. Matrix operations require compatible dimensions; square matrices may have determinants and inverses.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Algebra of Matrices; Determinant of Matrix; Solution of Simultaneous Equation (up to 3 variable); Determinants and Matrices. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-II problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

