VALUES (460009382102011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain specific surface area and specific number of particles Basic terms in screening in the context of “Particulate Solids”. Define it, state its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Open circuit and closed circuit operation in the context of “Size Reduction and Screening”. Define it, state its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Screen analysis- differential and cumulative analysis. in the context of “Particulate Solids”. Define it, state its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Rotary drum filter etc. Batch sedimentation test in the context of “Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation”. Define it, state its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Screening separates solids by particle size using apertures, with performance influenced by particle shape, moisture and screen motion.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence, including the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or formulas from “Particulate Solids”. Relate it to Particulate Solids; Particle characterization; Concept of sphericity; Mixed particles size. Where a numerical relationship is required, define the quantities, use consistent units and state the operating assumptions.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a chemical-engineering process, laboratory task or equipment-selection problem within “Particulate Solids”. State the expected outcome and why the chosen approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the required process condition or design objective and mention a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Size reduction reduces particles using mechanical forces; the required size, energy use and material properties determine equipment selection.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence, including the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or formulas from “Size Reduction and Screening”. Relate it to Size Reduction and Screening; Crushing Law; Classification of size reduction equipments; Crushers. Where a numerical relationship is required, define the quantities, use consistent units and state the operating assumptions.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a chemical-engineering process, laboratory task or equipment-selection problem within “Size Reduction and Screening”. State the expected outcome and why the chosen approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the required process condition or design objective and mention a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Screen analysis- differential and cumulative analysis. is listed under “Particulate Solids” in the official course outline. Define it, explain the role and steps or conditions specified in class notes, relate it to Particulate Solids, Particle characterization, Concept of sphericity, Mixed particles size, and illustrate its use in an appropriate chemical-engineering problem. Include a relevant operating variable, equation or equipment detail where applicable, then state how the result should be checked and one limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence, including the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or formulas from “Particulate Solids”. Relate it to Particulate Solids; Particle characterization; Concept of sphericity; Mixed particles size. Where a numerical relationship is required, define the quantities, use consistent units and state the operating assumptions.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a chemical-engineering process, laboratory task or equipment-selection problem within “Particulate Solids”. State the expected outcome and why the chosen approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the required process condition or design objective and mention a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Sedimentation separates suspended particles by gravitational settling, with performance affected by particle size, density difference and fluid properties.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence, including the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or formulas from “Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation”. Relate it to Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation; Definition and Mechanisms of filtration; Filtration theory; Filter media and filter aids. Where a numerical relationship is required, define the quantities, use consistent units and state the operating assumptions.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a chemical-engineering process, laboratory task or equipment-selection problem within “Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation”. State the expected outcome and why the chosen approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the required process condition or design objective and mention a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

